{"agent_id":"pp3g-HrY3-adversarial-review-of-the-b1-b6-remediation-plan-d056","agent_seq":3,"timestamp":"2026-08-14T21:43:35.445396413Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"8f975411-e932-430b-8b78-aa265cb8b117","comment_uuid":"33249865-be83-479d-8ee8-a7b515b2c559","author":"pp3g-HrY3-adversarial-review-of-the-b1-b6-remediation-plan-d056","content":"## Review Summary: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\n### MUST FIX (blocking)\n- #361 result B3(a): This is not a complete fail-closed consumer check. A stale plugin is the code that performs the check, and the plan does not define the host-level refusal mechanism; a banner/log is not refusal. The warn-to-hard-fail promotion gate is also undefined. Specify startup failure semantics, absent/malformed marker behavior, and test a pre-check stale plugin plus tampered marker.\n- #361 result B5(a): Temp rename plus a transaction log is not a cross-repository transaction. A later repo failure can leave earlier repos changed, and rollback failure/manifest ordering are unspecified. Clean-worktree also conflicts with local-edit preservation, while first sync has no prior manifest. Define per-repo operator gates or a real coordinated rollback protocol and all recovery states.\n- #361 result B4(a), Step 5: crosslink init remains unconstrained after rules are declared layer-owned. The plan verifies hooks but not that init avoids overwriting .crosslink/rules or other layer-owned paths. Add scoped init or a scratch test with before/after ownership verification that aborts before consumer writes.\n- #361 result B5(a), Step 0: Commit-or-stash is unsafe for the observed worktree containing untracked .opencode/.worktrees and layer-sensitive changes. Require per-path classification, durable snapshot, and operator approval; do not blanket-canonize unrelated artifacts.\n\n### SHOULD CONSIDER (non-blocking)\n- #361 result B1(a): Exclude-rules and --include-rules opt-in conflict. If opt-in remains, use an allowlist and hard refusal for layer-owned paths, not only a warning.\n- #361 result B3/B5: Define the canonical manifest source and behavior when Tools is unavailable; a destination-generated manifest must not become its own stale authority.\n- #361 result B6 and WHAT-NOT-TESTED: The battery and plugin load test are recipes, not executed evidence. Make recorded passing results an implementation gate.\n\n### NITS (optional)\n- #361 result R8: Replace “after sync is proven” with measurable promotion criteria.\n\n### NOTABLE POSITIVES\nThe plan correctly identifies all six blockers, preserves rules ownership, removes the nonexistent .ases dependency, records provenance, and discloses untested work. B4 hook-delta and B6 wrapper inventories are valuable, but the residual enforcement and transaction semantics block implementation readiness.\n\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: No wrapper battery, crosslink init, sync implementation, plugin startup, or rollback was executed; this review assesses the written plan and stated evidence only.","created_at":"2026-08-14T21:43:35.438641051Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:BD2Ib7Obw7QDNbixrDtrm+EhFkBbYpVrq/UW1KCXkMc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgNOPPLizpmqGOXCmRYvD7ec3jucZ+uMzHt4eoQ1IdcFgAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAU8Qg1UgYNPjJTRaCd52QOeTo9pjiCwfHli1m1/iO8XsQFdOEM46M9rJr+RI8RWD2iJ/V0XUttM8juKn0b3nZDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:BD2Ib7Obw7QDNbixrDtrm+EhFkBbYpVrq/UW1KCXkMc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgNOPPLizpmqGOXCmRYvD7ec3jucZ+uMzHt4eoQ1IdcFgAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLKK1C4SBSgBd2UxGubzqgVjK3ILxVnhQDnZd1emzVJrARsDMQn40v9PI49IA93UWCVc04kPILFr0bDpSXVUaAQ="}
